_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "5847a665e3d8835b0f7b5fc99a5435f269aed8ba5aac82bc9c4cc21d5f2bcba6" "basis" 1055 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (7+4{x}^{3}+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =3x-2\\pi ,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (7+4{x}^{3}+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7[1+{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi )])\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+7(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))+C \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{4}+\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "98846a7f0754c8f5e2c1765913fe44e07e9a2d340d587d1a3749b498ed3bcfc5" "basis" 1127 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}\n$$\n\n- The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=x$\n- The limit evaluates to $2$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$\n- The limit exists and is equal to $2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}=\\frac{2\\cdot {0}^{2}}{2\\cdot {0}^{2}-0}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{x(2x-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{2x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{2\\cdot 0-1} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is also true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "categ