01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the surface ${2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}=2.$ Given that $n=⟨a,b,c⟩$ is a non-zero normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,-1,1),$ what is the value of $\\frac{c}{b}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's define  $f(x,y,z)={2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}.$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=2.$  \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy})j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy})k \\\\  & =({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\cdot 2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)i+({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\cdot 2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)j+({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\cdot 6z\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)k \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(y\\,\\text{ }{2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\text{ }i+x\\,\\text{ }{2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\text{ }j+3z\\,\\text{ }{2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\text{ }k) \\\\ ∇f(1,-1,1) & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2((-1)\\cdot \\text{ }{2}^{3(1)^{2}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)}\\text{ }i+1\\cdot \\,\\text{ }{2}^{3(1)^{2}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)}\\text{ }j+3(1)\\cdot {2}^{3(1)^{2}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)}\\text{ }k) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(-{2}^{1}\\text{ }i+{2}^{1}\\text{ }j+3\\cdot {2}^{1}\\text{ }k) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(-i+j+3\\text{ }k) \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,12\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩=⟨-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,12\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{c}{b}=\\frac{12\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c388c1ed8737218b3f157b217ff4731b172ace8aed19307b31a77aa2ed9997c6" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.ty