1b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}49 & -8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-111083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd53e7bf7d5" "basis" 2523 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-111083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y<2) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(0,1),(1,1),(1,2),(2,1)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,1))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & =f(0,1)+f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.25+0.1+0.25 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070542/state.json" "file_sha256" "01c01a26e01298a5b694130ac4e21b96a9528a36eca715d82138edd